<idea-plugin>
  <id>com.github.khopland.emberkai</id>
  <name>Emberkai Theme</name>
  <vendor url="https://github.com/khopland/emberkai-intellij">khopland</vendor>
  <depends>com.intellij.modules.lang</depends>

  <description>
  <![CDATA[
  <p>Emberkai is a dark theme collection for IntelliJ-based IDEs.</p>
  <p>Choose from five palettes: Default, Machine, Octagon, Ristretto, and
  Spectrum. Each uses the Islands layout, with a Contrast option for
  brighter secondary text and Teal and Rose accents.</p>
  <p>Includes optional No Italics editor schemes, coordinated diff and console
  colors, and palette-matched semantic highlighting for parameters and local
  variables. Semantic highlighting is off by default.</p>
  <p>Requires IntelliJ Platform 2025.3 or newer. Select a theme under
  Settings &gt; Appearance &amp; Behavior &gt; Appearance.</p>
  <p><a href="https://github.com/khopland/emberkai-intellij/issues">Report an issue</a> |
  <a href="https://github.com/khopland/emberkai-intellij">Source code</a> |
  <a href="https://github.com/khopland/emberkai-intellij/blob/main/LICENSE">Apache 2.0 license</a></p>
  <p>Theme color credits:
  <a href="https://github.com/tautastic/neokai">Neokai by tautastic</a> and
  <a href="https://github.com/espositocode/monokai-pro">Monokai Pro Theme 1.10 by Subtheme</a>.</p>
  ]]>
  </description>

  <change-notes>
  <![CDATA[
  <p>1.0.0 — Initial Emberkai release.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Five Islands palettes with Contrast variants and Teal and Rose accents.</li>
    <li>Matching No Italics editor schemes.</li>
    <li>Coordinated diff, console, and optional semantic highlighting colors.</li>
  </ul>
  ]]>
  </change-notes>

